# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
/data
dist
.env
.env.*
src-tauri/target
dist-ssr
*.local

# ─── Belt-and-suspenders: never commit runtime / user data ──────────────────
# /data (above) already covers the dev data directory where these normally
# live. These extra patterns catch a sensitive file even if a stray copy ever
# ended up somewhere else in the tree (e.g. dragged to the repo root to inspect
# it). The .enc envelopes and the lock hash are the crown jewels — losing those
# to a public commit is the one outcome worth being paranoid about.
*.enc
lock.json
budget-*.json
time-tracker.json
draft.json
settings.json
*-settings.json
custom-themes.json
shell-state.json
window.json
auto-backup.json
auto-backup-presets.json
backups/

# Atomic-write temp files (pid-tagged) and tool outputs, in case any were ever
# produced inside the repo during testing.
*.tmp-*
robocopy_log_*.txt
files-generated-*/
resized-*/

# Build-generated copies in public/ (created by copy-public-docs.mjs —
# the originals at the repo root are the tracked source of truth)
public/README.md
public/LICENSE
public/LICENSE.md
public/ATTRIBUTION.md
public/CHANGELOG.json
public/CONTRIBUTING.md
public/SECURITY.md
public/swiss-rb-knife-logo.png
public/screenshots/

# Tauri-generated schemas (regenerated on every dev/build)
src-tauri/gen/schemas

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Windows junk
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini